    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b5032d00_a267a3c0",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 5065
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-11-09T16:03:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I see your point, but we\u0027ll need it if Chrome wants to insert readPixels into a Recording. I\u0027d rather have everything flow through one place, even if it\u0027s heavy-handed in some cases (it\u0027s already heavy-handed since we have to sync). If we can convince Chrome to do everything through the Context then I don\u0027t see a need for a Recorder.",
      "parentUuid": "68c5b31e_3577b280",
      "revId": "543ae28d9a2c3d6b7c1d2e2db8666f50c6a0b909",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e8b7f047_755ebbd0",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 5036
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-11-09T16:23:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So if we do that would we be moving all of the code currently in Context::asyncReadPixels into the Recorder? Or are there things we want to keep separate/different between the Context::asyncReadPixel calls and the Recorder::asyncReadPixels call? If we want those two functions to be different, maybe it makes more sense to just have a utility function that produces the copy and sync tasks. Then both recorder and context could just call that helper to generate the tasks and Context wouldn\u0027t need a Recorder.\n\nIf we do go the approach where everything is in the recorder, then Context should be making a long lived recorder to reuse so we can reuse the buffer allocations.",
      "parentUuid": "b5032d00_a267a3c0",
      "revId": "543ae28d9a2c3d6b7c1d2e2db8666f50c6a0b909",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c531198c_5a981f67",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 5036
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-11-09T16:29:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I guess in short my opinion is, as of right now we don\u0027t have support for calling asyncReadPixels from a Recorder. It all goes through context (ignoring testing backdoor, but that still ends up at context). So in today\u0027s world we should just have all the read pixel logic in Context. The Recorder doesn\u0027t add anything but extra layers. If we then later decide we do need to support asyncReadPixels on Recorder then we can move all of the logic off Context and onto Recorder for everything to use.\n\nAlternatively we could try to figure out from Chrome beforehand, now why they think that need the Recorder API and if that\u0027s actually a valid reason to add the more complex API (more complex since we need the multiple callbacks for release and \"never call release again\" procs).",
      "parentUuid": "e8b7f047_755ebbd0",
      "revId": "543ae28d9a2c3d6b7c1d2e2db8666f50c6a0b909",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
